    'Labels fans use to identify themselves and the groups they build with.' => '粉丝用来称呼自己和所在团体的说法。',
    'Names for the individual elements you actually snap together.' => '你实际拼在一起的各种零件的名称。',
    'Names for set lines, exclusives, and what happens when a set retires.' => '关于产品线、独家套装以及套装停产的说法。',
    'Vocabulary for how AFOLs actually put bricks together.' => 'AFOL 拼搭积木时用到的词汇。',
    'Vocabulary that pops up on resale sites and trade forums.' => '转卖网站和交易论坛上常见的词汇。',
    'Apps, databases and acronyms from around the LEGO ecosystem.' => '乐高生态中的应用、数据库和缩写。',
    'An adult LEGO enthusiast, usually 18+, who actively follows the hobby.' => '积极参与这项爱好的成年乐高粉丝，通常在 18 岁以上。',
    'A teenage LEGO fan, usually 13–17. The bridge between KFOL and AFOL.' => '青少年乐高粉丝，通常为 13–17 岁，介于 KFOL 和 AFOL 之间。',
    'A child LEGO fan, the original target audience for most retail sets.' => '儿童乐高粉丝，大多数零售套装最初的目标群体。',
    'An adult female LEGO fan. Used when distinguishing the demographic; otherwise AFOL covers everyone.' => '成年女性乐高粉丝。用于区分这一群体，其他情况下 AFOL 涵盖所有人。',
    'A community of AFOLs that meets locally or online to build and share the hobby.' => '在线下或线上聚会、一起拼搭和分享爱好的 AFOL 团体。',
    'A LUG officially recognized by The LEGO Group, eligible for support like exclusive sets for events.' => '获得乐高集团官方认可的 LUG，可获得支持，例如活动用的独家套装。',
    'The official channel through which TLG communicates with recognized LUGs and ambassadors worldwide.' => 'TLG 与全球认可的 LUG 和大使沟通的官方渠道。',
    'The Danish company that designs and manufactures LEGO products.' => '设计和制造乐高产品的丹麦公司。',
    'The classic rectangular element with studs on top. The building block of every LEGO set (e.g. 2x4, 1x2).' => '顶部带凸点的经典长方形零件，每个乐高套装的基础（如 2x4、1x2）。',
    'A flat element one third of a brick’s height. Three stacked plates equal the height of one brick.' => '高度为砖块三分之一的扁平零件。三块板叠起来等于一块砖的高度。',
    'A flat element with no studs on top, used for smooth surfaces, floors, and details.' => '顶部没有凸点的扁平零件，用于平滑表面、地板和细节。',
    'The cylindrical bump on top of a brick or plate that allows pieces to snap together.' => '砖块或板顶部的圆柱形凸起，让零件可以拼合在一起。',
    'An angled element used for roofs, ramps and other non-flat surfaces.' => '用于屋顶、坡道等非平面的斜面零件。',
    'A tiny 1x1 sloped piece named for its wedge shape; a workhorse for greebling and small details.' => '形似一块楔形奶酪的 1x1 小斜面零件，是增加细节和表面装饰的好帮手。',
    'A plate with a single centered stud, used to offset other parts by half a stud.' => '中间只有一个凸点的板，用于让其他零件偏移半个凸点。',
    'A large thin plate that serves as the foundation for a build. Not stackable like regular plates.' => '作为作品底座的大薄板，不能像普通板那样叠放。',
    'A small set (usually under 100 pieces) sold in a sealed plastic bag instead of a box. Often promotional.' => '装在密封塑料袋而不是盒子里的小套装（通常少于 100 颗粒），常作为促销品。',
    'A Star Wars line of large, display-focused sets aimed at adult collectors, often with high piece counts.' => '面向成年收藏者的大型展示类星球大战系列，颗粒数通常很多。',
    'A premium set distributed mainly via LEGO.com and brand stores rather than mass-market retailers.' => '主要通过 LEGO.com 和乐高品牌店而非大众零售商销售的高端套装。',
    'A small bonus set given free with qualifying orders, typically time-limited and used to drive sales.' => '订单满一定金额即可免费获得的小赠品套装，通常限时。',
    'LEGO’s free loyalty program: earn points on purchases, redeem for sets, GWPs, or experiences.' => '乐高的免费会员计划：购物积累积分，可兑换套装、赠品或体验。',
    'An adult-oriented line of stackable city buildings (32x32 stud footprint) that connect side by side.' => '面向成人的可叠放城市建筑系列（底座 32x32 凸点），可以并排拼接。',
    'A mini-build polybag bundled with a collectible LEGO magazine at newsstands and kiosks.' => '随报亭出售的乐高收藏杂志附赠的袋装迷你模型。',
    'A set sold only through official LEGO channels (LEGO.com, brand stores) and not via mass retailers.' => '仅通过乐高官方渠道（LEGO.com、乐高品牌店）销售、不在大众零售商出售的套装。',
    'A set officially out of production. Stock dries up and aftermarket prices tend to climb.' => '已正式停产的套装。库存减少后，二手价格往往会上涨。',
    'A set scheduled for retirement. Once EOL is reached, no more units will be produced.' => '计划停产的套装。到期后将不再生产。',
    'A small set distributed as a giveaway, contest prize, or partnership bonus rather than retail sale.' => '作为赠品、比赛奖品或合作福利发放，而非零售的小套装。',
    'A model designed and built from scratch by a fan, not based on any official LEGO set.' => '由粉丝从零开始设计和拼搭、不基于任何官方套装的作品。',
    'A family of techniques that orient studs sideways or downward, used for smooth surfaces and unusual angles.' => '让凸点朝向侧面或下方的一类技巧，用于平滑表面和特殊角度。',
    'A pre-assembled element (like a pre-printed wall section) replacing what builders would rather construct themselves. Generally seen as a negative.' => '一种预先成型的零件（如印刷好的墙面），取代了拼搭者更想自己拼出来的部分。通常被视为缺点。',
    'A large, single-mold rock element. Disliked because it removes the chance to build rocks from smaller parts.' => '一体成型的大型岩石零件。不受欢迎，因为无法再用小零件拼出岩石。',
    'Adding small decorative parts (pipes, antennas, gears) to make a surface look busy and technical. Popular on spaceships.' => '添加管子、天线、齿轮等小装饰零件，让表面显得复杂有科技感。常用于宇宙飞船。',
    'Building at a scale much smaller than minifigure scale, e.g. a whole castle that fits in your palm.' => '以远小于人仔比例的尺寸拼搭，例如一座能放在掌心的城堡。',
    'The default scale (roughly 1:42) where models are sized for minifigures to interact with.' => '标准比例（约 1:42），模型尺寸与人仔相配。',
    'A connection that works but violates LEGO’s internal design rules (e.g. stressing a part). Common in fan MOCs, rare in official sets.' => '能拼上但违反乐高内部设计规则的连接方式（例如让零件受力）。在粉丝作品中常见，在官方套装中很少。',
    'The largest online marketplace for LEGO parts, minifigures, and sets, also home to the Stud.io builder.' => '最大的乐高零件、人仔和套装在线交易市场，也是 Stud.io 软件的出品方。',
    'A set still factory-sealed in its original box, in pristine condition. Commands the highest resale prices.' => '仍保持出厂密封、原盒完好的套装，转卖价格最高。',
    'A set that has never been opened. Often used interchangeably with MISB.' => '从未拆封的套装，常与 MISB 互换使用。',
    'A complete set with original box, but the seal may be broken. Lower value than MISB/NISB.' => '带原盒的完整套装，但封条可能已破，价值低于 MISB/NISB。',
    'Official LEGO stores (LEGO.com and physical brand stores). The primary source for exclusives and GWPs.' => '乐高官方商店（LEGO.com 和实体品牌店），独家套装和赠品的主要来源。',
    'The price a set commands on the secondary market after retiring from retail. Often used to track sets as investments.' => '套装停止零售后在二手市场上的价格，常用于把套装当作投资来追踪。',
    'A set bought primarily because it’s expected to grow in value after retirement, rather than to build.' => '主要因为预期停产后会升值而购买、并非为了拼搭的套装。',
    'An open standard and library of part files for digital LEGO models. The foundation of most third-party CAD tools.' => '用于数字乐高模型的开放标准和零件库，大多数第三方 CAD 工具的基础。',
    'A free LEGO CAD program from BrickLink with rendering, building instructions and a parts-ordering flow.' => 'BrickLink 推出的免费乐高 CAD 软件，支持渲染、生成拼搭说明和订购零件。',
    'LEGO’s official (now discontinued) CAD program. Replaced in the community by Stud.io.' => '乐高官方的 CAD 软件（现已停止更新），社区中已被 Stud.io 取代。',
    'A community database of sets, parts, and minifigures, with alternate-build instructions for parts you already own.' => '社区维护的套装、零件和人仔数据库，还提供用你现有零件拼的替代模型说明。',
    'A long-running set database with reviews, news, prices, and collection-tracking tools for AFOLs.' => '历史悠久的套装数据库，为 AFOL 提供评测、新闻、价格和收藏管理工具。',
    'A competing brick brand (e.g. COBI, Mega Construx) producing LEGO-compatible elements. Generally not considered "LEGO".' => '生产乐高兼容零件的竞争品牌（如 COBI、Mega Construx），通常不被视为“乐高”。',
